                               Package
                                  
     File_Id.Diz - short product description for BBS/sites operators
     History.Eng - English development history
     History.Rus - Russian development history
     SHELLINK.DLL - FAR plugin itself
     shellink.inf - installation script
     ReadMe.Eng - English manual (this file)
     LinkEng.hlf - English help file
     LinkRus.hlf - Russian help file
     LinkEng.lng - plugins' messages in English
     LinkRus.lng - plugins' messages in Russian
     ReadMe.Rus - Russian manual
     Here  and  further the term "English" only means  the  language
that  the  author used writing those documents and, therefore,  this
language  version can be different from classic one. The  author  is
not a writer, but reader.
                                  
                      Installation and running
                                  
     First  of  all, if the product package is an archive file,  you
should extract that archive into a temporary folder. Then choose  an
appropriate way of installation, one of described below.
     
Standard installation
     
     Close  all active copies of FAR. Use Windows Explorer to  enter
to  the folder containing package files. Click right mouse button on
shellink.inf file, then choose "Install" item of popup  menu.  Shell
link     support    plugin    files    will    be    copied     into
Program   Files\Far\Plugins\SHELLINK   directory.   Default   plugin
settings     will    be    placed    into    the    registry     key
HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Far\Plugins\OS\ShellLinker.
     
Manual installation
     
     Create  the subfolder ShelLink in the folder Plugins  that,  in
its  turn,  should  be  placed  in your  FAR  folder.  Copy  to  the
Far\Plugins\ShelLink  directory  all  the  files  mentioned  in  the
package description above.
     You  can  give  another name to the shell link  support  plugin
folder,  and  you not must to create it; but all the  components  of
this plugin should be visible to FAR.
     In  this  case, default plugin settings are stored  in  program
body  until a first change when they are imported into the  registry
key    HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Far\Plugins\OS\ShellLinker.   Then
plugin uses values kept under this key.
     
Running
     
     When  you  installed the plugin, restart FAR. New  item  "Shell
link  creation"  will  appear in "Plugin commands"  list  called  by
pressing  <F11>  key,  and item "Shell link  support  options"  will
appear in "Options/Plugin configuration" menu.
                                  
                            Uninstalling
                                  
     Close all active copies of FAR before you uninstall shell  link
support plugin. Then do your did using one of next ways.
     
Standard uninstalling
     
     If  you  installed plugin with installation script, go  to  the
Control  Panel and choose "Add/Remove program" item.  Then  find  in
installed applications list "FAR plugin - Shell file and folder link
support"  string,  mark it and press "Add/Remove"  button.  All  the
plugin files and registry keys will be deleted.
     
Manual uninstalling
     
     Delete  the  folder where you placed shell link support  plugin
files.                         Registry                          key
HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Far\Plugins\OS\ShellLinker also  must  be
deleted. You are responsible to do this work correctly.
                                  
                               Basics
                                  
     A shell link is a data object that contains information used to
access  another  object  in  the shell's namespace  such  as  files,
folders,  disk drives, and printers. Shell link itself, in the  most
cases,  is  a  file  system object or, simply, file,  and  its  name
includes  .lnk extension; at this point, terms "link" and "shortcut"
are equal.
     To  gain  access to linked object shell link must  be  resolved
using  either  MS  Windows Explorer or any other file  manager  that
should  call  suitable Windows API functions.  When  the  object  is
found,  file manager can perfom some actions associated with  object
of this type.
     Shell  link  have some standart properties such as  icon,  work
directory,  command  string arguments (link to  executable  module),
description - that can be changed, and the set can be extended; file
manager should do this work too.
     Shell link support FAR plugin is intended to create shell links
to  objects  visible  in FAR file panels, i.e.  files  and  folders.
Additional  feature is the changing current panel folder  to  linked
one, when link resolved is a folder shortcut. Shell link file can be
created  either on desktop (in its folder), or in another FAR  panel
current folder.
     It  is  impossible to create shortcut to an emulated by another
plugin file system object with help of this plugin because such link
is definitly unresolvable. However shell link to a network resource -
  file or folder - represented by the network browser plugin can  be
created.
     Shell   link  support  FAR  plugin  performs  no  any   editing
facilities for already existing shell links, so Explorer do it  much
better.  At least, the author had not found any arguments  for  this
idea.
                                  
                               Reasons
                                  
     It  is often necessary to create shortcut on desktop or in main
menu  to  a file in a big depth situated (from 4th level and deeper)
subfolder.  Sure,  you  can  switch to desktop,  press  right  mouse
button,  call  shortcut  creation wizard... and  again,  you  should
search the file that is already under cursor in FAR panel!
     Make the task more complex. A group of shortcuts to a few files
from one subfolder is to be created on desktop. It means you have to
repeat  the set of same routine operations for a few times.  Or  you
can create one shortcut, when copy and change, change, change...
     Laziness makes the world go around, ain't it?
                                  
                                Using
                                  
Configuration
     
     When  you  enter  the  menu "Options/Plugin configuration"  and
choose the item "Shell link support options", the dialog appears and
you can change these parameters.
Resolve folder links            This   checkbox   defines,   is   it
                                possible  to  change  current  panel
                                folder  to  linked one  by  pressing
                                <Enter> on shell link file or not
                                
Folder link mask                File  mask  or set of masks  divided
                                by   commas.  Plugin  considers  any
                                file  matched  as a  shell  link  to
                                folder  and,  therefore,  tries   to
                                resolve it.
                                
Description prefix              This  text  is  a constant  part  of
                                description  of newly created  shell
                                link
                                
Create shell links by default:  This buttons define default path  to
                                newly created shell link file:
                                
On panel                        in another panel current folder
                                
On desktop                      in desktop folder
     
     These   parameters   are   kept   under   the   registry    key
HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Far\Plugins\OS\ShellLinker,    but    you
should not correct them there without special necessity.
     
Shell link creation
     
     Set the file panel cursor to the object you need or select some
object,  press  <F11>  key  or  choose  menu  item  "Commands/Plugin
commands",  then choose list item "Shell link creation". Before  the
shortcut  (or  group of shortcuts) will be created, you  can  change
these its properties.
     
Where                           Path  to  shell link file -  desktop
                                or    another   panel   folder    by
                                default  -  and its name  consisting
                                of object name and .lnk extension
                                
Description                     Shell  link  description  consisting
                                of  configuration  defined  constant
                                part and object name
     
     Default  values  of these fields are defined in  dialog  "Shell
link support options".
     When  group of shortcuts is created, field {Where} must contain
path only and field {Description} must contain constant part only.
     Press  <Create> button when you agree with values entered,  and
shell link will be created in {Where} placeholder.
     If  link file supposed to be created on desktop by default, you
can create it in another panel folder by pressing <On panel> button.
Vice  versa,  pressing <On desktop> button changes destination  path
from another panel folder to desktop one.
     You  can  change link file name case by pressing <Case> button.
The order is "File name.Ext" -> "File Name.Ext" -> "FILE NAME.EXT" -
> "file name.ext", one step by time.
     If  shell  link file with such name already exists,  you'll  be
asked to overwrite it or to cancel operation.
     
Folder link resolution
     
     Shell link support plugin allows to change current panel folder
to  linked one by pressing <Enter> key on shell link file,  if  it's
not a link to another type object.
     This  feature can be turned off , if you wish, in dialog "Shell
link support options".
                                  
